~ initialize_local_variables

=> start

~ start
A frail fragment: *joan eyes closed* Consciousness kicks in. You find yourself at the village gates, barely able to stand, feet all swollen and bloody. 
A frail fragment: Your eyes and your entire body feel heavy, like they haven't known sleep for weeks. You smell horrible. 
A frail fragment: How long has it been? Have you been walking this whole time, no rest, no food, no water to drink?
A frail fragment: In spite of everything, you feel something you can't quite understand. A sense of... accomplishment, a warmth that fills you with unprecedented joy.
A frail fragment: You need nothing. You crave nothing. All you want is to get through those gates. 
A frail fragment: You can vaguely make someone's eyes out through what you can only assume is a sliding peephole. They watch as you walk towards them. 
A frail fragment: ...After what feels like too long, you hear a sickly, croaking, womanly voice. *eyes open*
=> END

